module agentic

# ========================================
# EVAL RUN TYPE (Agent- or plugin-bound)
# ========================================
# One run of test cases on an agent, or on a plugin on the built-in
# assistant, optionally with and without a plugin.
#
# Authorization model:
# - Exactly one subject parent is written: the agent or the plugin (the
#   spec's subject oneof; the kind's two optional parents). Every relation
#   below reads both, and the one never written contributes nothing.
# - The subject's editors start, cancel and delete its eval runs, as an
#   agent's editors own its evaluator.
# - The subject's viewers in the subject's own organization read the eval
#   run and, through the session link (session#eval_run), its tries. A
#   child organization's viewer of a shared agent or plugin does not: a try
#   spends the subject organization's money and may act with its
#   connections. The model has no `but not`, so agent.fga and plugin.fga
#   name that set `org_viewer`.
# - A compared plugin is no parent: deleting it leaves an agent's eval runs
#   and their results, and its viewers read nothing through it.
# - No owner of its own (OWNER_ATTRIBUTION_TYPE_NONE). The subject's owner
#   already includes the organization's admins, who hold the purse the
#   eval run spends.

type eval_run
  relations
    # ========================================
    # ORGANIZATION
    # ========================================
    define organization: [organization]

    # ========================================
    # SUBJECT (exactly one written)
    # ========================================
    # FGA tuple: eval_run:<id>#agent@agent:<agent_id>
    define agent: [agent]
    # FGA tuple: eval_run:<id>#plugin@plugin:<plugin_id>
    define plugin: [plugin]

    # ========================================
    # OPERATIONS
    # ========================================
    define viewer: org_viewer from agent or org_viewer from plugin
    define can_view: viewer
    define can_edit: can_edit from agent or can_edit from plugin
    define can_delete: can_edit from agent or can_edit from plugin
